        "tree_id": "99f4c985d2dadaee6e1efe97521f655347c8f2f9",
        "message": "Restore the full client UI and gate the build with contract tests\n\nThe nine Swift files that implement the dashboard, feature store, lockout,\nsensitivity lookup and app config existed on disk but were never added to the\napp target, so they compiled nowhere and the shipped IPA had no aimlock\nassist screen. They are now in the Sources phase (22 files), and\ntools/check_swift_sources.py fails the build when disk and target disagree.\n\nAlongside the restore: the legal document reader, the welcome greeting with a\ntwo-hour snooze, endpoint obfuscation tables, and static contract tests that\npin the Worker surface, the eight feature ids, the no-fake-button rule, and\nSwift syntax (tree-sitter) in CI.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
        "timestamp": "2026-11-12T11:33:26Z",
        "author": {
          "name": "thait2471-sys",
          "email": "thait2471@gmail.com"
        },
